    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a lineup anchored by two elite projections: **Trea Turner** (70.26) and **Christian Yelich** (69.63). **Trea Turner** benefits significantly from a favorable #1 spot in the order (+10%) and a positive historical BvP profile against the opposing right-hander, while **Christian Yelich** capitalizes on a strong platoon advantage (+13%) and a projected wind-aided environment to maximize his run-scoring potential. **Kyle Schwarber** (64.77) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (63.35) also present high-upside plays; **Pete Crow-Armstrong** remains a primary target due to his lead-off role, providing a stable floor even in the absence of a confirmed opposing pitcher, while **Kyle Schwarber** maintains his value through a prime #2 batting slot despite the challenge of facing a tough arm in Sandy Alcantara.\n\nThe decision to limit the bench was tight, with **Josh Smith** (44.21) presenting the most compelling case for inclusion. **Josh Smith** was ultimately squeezed out by the depth of the outfield and utility slots, as the optimizer favored the platoon-adjusted ceiling of **Lars Nootbaar** (56.41) and the raw power profile of **Yordan Alvarez** (53.45). While **Yordan Alvarez** faces a difficult L/L matchup against Reid Detmers, his elite 0.474 xwOBA keeps him firmly above the replacement threshold compared to the bench options. Note that all projections remain subject to the \"Lineup Pending\" volatility; should the confirmed lineups shift significantly, the aggressive starts for **Dillon Dingler** and **Kazuma Okamoto**\u2014who both carry scores in the mid-40s\u2014could become precarious if their batting positions drop lower than the anticipated #2 and #6 spots, respectively.",
